    "result": "I implemented `search_products` in `solution.py` to match the spec, and the 14 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass.\n\n- **Name search:** it matches with `instr(lower(name), lower(?))`, so `%` and `_` are plain characters and matching is case-insensitive for ASCII.\n- **Ordering and paging:** `ORDER BY <name|price> ASC/DESC, id ASC` followed by `LIMIT`/`OFFSET`, with `id` ascending breaking ties in both directions.\n- **Validation:** a bad `order_by`, `limit` or `offset` raises `ValueError`. I also reject booleans for `limit` and `offset`, which the spec doesn't mention.\n- **Read-only:** the function only runs a `SELECT`.\n\nOne assertion in `test_name_binary_order` ends in `or True`, so it can never fail. The check that follows it (names come back sorted) does run.",
